s  were throwing things at the officers and  that may have been one of the causes but  we're still evaluating the situation so  those that are being detained and  arrested or do our mainly doing so or  they're being arrested for violating a  dispersal order so at the end of the day  if we've offered and we've given many  many opportunities for the protesters to  disperse the only time that this  personal order is given is if they  become unruly and start violating other  laws so violating traffic laws or  harming officers or harming other  citizens anything of the sort that would  be a violation of the law and a safety  matter at that point we would issue a  dispersal order we usually give multiple  dispersal orders wait enough time for  people to leave a lot of law-abiding  citizens that just want to protest  peacefully they do leave and they don't  want anything to do with the violence  they just want to be here and express  their First Amendment rights those that  stay and want to continue to violate the  law those are the ones that arrested  we've done our best to be in contact  with those organizing but this tonight's  event had a mixture of different groups  that were here we don't believe that  there was just one person responsible  for organizing this entire event but we  have tried our best to communicate with  those individuals express our concerns  also our solidarity and where we stand  with supporting some of the issues that  are happening right now across the  country but ultimately some of that  communication only goes to certain  people and then others who don't  necessarily care to to communicate with  the police have moved forward with what  they did tonight  I'm sorry I don't have any information  on that but I can tell you with  confidence that we only arrest those  individuals who are breaking the law and  in addition when they're breaking the  law in this particular case it's because  it's also a safety issue there have been  some individuals who were initially  detained and then cited and released but  a lot of the other individuals are being  arrested and going to jail because of  the level of violation or the level of  violence that escalated later through  the night but I just like to just again  remind the community that we will  certainly support everyone's First  Amendment rights or any other  constitutional protected activities we  encourage people to continue to if they  want a protest to protest peacefully but  at the same time we have to protect our  community we've formed this concept of  Vegas strong and it's important that we  embody that to protect all of our  community including our police officers  including the public that's out there so  please just those that are out there  continue to obey the law and we'll do  the best we can to support you thank you  you
 

